1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
- www.addic7ed.com -

2
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:11,762
Brothers and sisters,
behold, I tell you a mystery.

3
00:00:12,221 --> 00:00:14,806
We shall not all fall asleep,

4
00:00:15,224 --> 00:00:18,936
but we will all be
changed in an instant,

5
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:22,189
in the blink of an eye,
at the last trumpet.

6
00:00:23,232 --> 00:00:25,067
For the trumpet will sound

7
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:28,862
and the dead will be
raised incorruptible,

8
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,281
and we shall be changed.

9
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:34,952
Almighty God,

10
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:39,373
remember the mercy with which
you graced your humble servant.

11
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:44,836
Receive her, we pray, into
the mansions of the saints.

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:48,590
As we prepare our
sister's final resting,

13
00:00:48,674 --> 00:00:51,927
look also with love on those who mourn

14
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:54,680
and give them comfort in their loss.

15
00:00:55,847 --> 00:01:00,143
Grant this through
Christ, our Lord, Amen.

16
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:01,812
Amen.

17
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:52,946
- Madam President, can I ride with you?
- Of course.

18
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:47,477
Has he approached you?

19
00:03:49,146 --> 00:03:50,146
Who?

20
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,189
Petrov.

21
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,820
Didn't he just arrive?

22
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:01,032
If the talks on Syria have
broken down, what's he doing here?

23
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,994
It's either a good thing or a bad thing.

24
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,705
Well, which is it?

25
00:04:08,874 --> 00:04:10,125
Madam President?

26
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,378
He was fond of Cathy.

27
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:23,388
I need to know that you won't
stand in the way of my handling...

28
00:04:23,472 --> 00:04:25,974
Mark. It's done.

29
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,267
You won.

30
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,860
It was necessary to show you,

31
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:38,570
but not what I wanted.

32
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,614
I don't know what you're talking about.

33
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:44,451
You did that to both of us. You did it.

34
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,330
You involved me, you implicated me.

35
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,210
- You left him in my house.
- Mark, that's enough.

36
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,505
It doesn't matter anymore.

37
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:10,685
Stan, my deepest condolences.

38
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:15,732
This is Cathy's brother
Hunter. He flew in from Eugene.

39
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:18,276
Just outside Lane County.

40
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,070
Beautiful country out there.

41
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:23,740
I was planning to come out anyway.

42
00:05:24,783 --> 00:05:26,451
Stan's birthday is on the sixth.

43
00:05:26,535 --> 00:05:27,828
Cathy and I have been...

44
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,913
back and forth for months.

45
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,873
I'm so sorry for your loss.

46
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:36,837
- Doug, this is Cathy's brother Hunter.
- Hi.

47
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,397
- Hey.
- And you've met Stan.

48
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,423
- Of course.
- Thank you for coming.

49
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:44,928
Doug, I think, spent more
time with Cathy than anyone.

50
00:05:45,846 --> 00:05:47,180
She didn't deserve this.

51
00:05:48,265 --> 00:05:50,141
Honestly, it doesn't seem real.

52
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,480
Would you excuse me?

53
00:05:58,233 --> 00:05:59,651
What time did she die?

54
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,529
I don't...

55
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:04,948
Sorry, I know it's a
weird question. I just...

56
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,908
I had one of those feelings that day.

57
00:06:08,285 --> 00:06:12,038
Um... 5:43, I think.

58
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:14,958
Yeah, right around then.

59
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,587
Mr. President.

60
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:20,255
President Underwood.

61
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:24,509
Secretary Durant was
from a time that's passed.

62
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,386
Holbrooke, Albright...

63
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:29,139
They knew how to have a good meal
and some friendly conversation

64
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,016
before diplomacy got ugly.

65
00:06:32,517 --> 00:06:34,728
It certainly won't be
the same without her.

66
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:38,440
I hear they have you on a short leash.

67
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:41,610
How could you let that
happen, Madam President?

68
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:45,655
Now, when we're only
moments away from crisis.

69
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,576
You know, in some cultures

70
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:53,038
it occurs to them to
actually honor the dead.

71
00:06:54,623 --> 00:06:56,750
Every seven years the Malagasy people

72
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:59,336
exhume the bones,
wrapping them in cloth,

73
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:01,546
so they can dance with the bodies.

74
00:07:02,923 --> 00:07:06,176
How does this town rise to the occasion?

75
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:10,472
It's like their heads are on a swivel.

76
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:15,268
Yeah. What do you call those things?

77
00:07:15,352 --> 00:07:16,561
Bobble heads?

78
00:07:17,938 --> 00:07:18,939
Terrifying.

79
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:21,900
No, don't... Let her be.

80
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:27,197
You wanted her to play the part.

81
00:07:28,031 --> 00:07:29,199
Voilà.

82
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:32,410
- The president.
- The president is too agreeable.

83
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:34,996
What did you do to her?

84
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:38,416
I trust her contempt more
than whatever this is.

85
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,460
Love, I know what you're capable of.

86
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:43,337
Hey.

87
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,384
DIA believes there are
over 100,000 Russian troops

88
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:49,761
- on their way to the border.
- Did you find Bugayev?

89
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:52,555
As of a few minutes ago, his
second in command assured me

90
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:55,558
that was the last contact we would
have from anyone at the Kremlin.

91
00:07:56,518 --> 00:07:57,936
Except for him.

92
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:01,539
He's requesting a private
meeting with the president.

93
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:03,775
- Sure.
- God damn it.

94
00:08:04,442 --> 00:08:06,778
- Mr. President.
- Mr. Vice President.

95
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,488
You know Secretary Siegerson.

96
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,573
- Yes. Of course.
- So good to see you.

97
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:13,868
Madam President, excuse me.

98
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:16,287
Oh, yes. Excuse me a moment.

99
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:17,414
Of course.

100
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:20,875
Cathy was kind to me.

101
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:24,212
A role model. Sensible, shrewd.

102
00:08:24,546 --> 00:08:26,006
Fluent in French.

103
00:08:26,631 --> 00:08:28,091
Rest in peace.

104
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:31,720
I know it's not the place, but...

105
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,140
this isn't normal, what's going on.

106
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:38,810
When I accepted my position, it was
to work with you and your agenda,

107
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:39,894
not...

108
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,478
not...

109
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:46,651
Certain members of our Cabinet

110
00:08:46,735 --> 00:08:48,737
in positions related
to National Security

111
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:51,614
have had several secret
meetings regarding Syria.

112
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,742
President Petrov has become aware

113
00:08:53,825 --> 00:08:57,037
of their plans for sending
private contractors to the region.

114
00:08:57,495 --> 00:08:58,495
Ma'am...

115
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:01,082
there are officials in the Pentagon,

116
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,543
people at the Kremlin, who
would very much like to prevent

117
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:06,463
- a proxy war...
- Nora, I appreciate your candor,

118
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:08,298
but Mark has this.

119
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:10,258
Ma'am, the Cabinet is his.

120
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:11,843
He knows what we need to do.

121
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:18,975
What makes me suspect
you're vying for speaker is

122
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:20,894
the frontrunners change day to day,

123
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:23,063
but everybody's second
choice remains the same.

124
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:25,148
- You.
- Brett, are you saying you wouldn't do it,

125
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,357
if the party asked?

126
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:28,401
If the party knew
what was good for them.

127
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:31,863
This is Douglas Stamper. He's
coming on as a consultant.

128
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,323
We've met.

129
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:35,200
Jonah, back when Francis was whip,

130
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:38,244
and you, back when you
were getting us coffee.

131
00:09:38,328 --> 00:09:40,246
I do wonder how he'd feel with some

132
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:44,334
of the legislation the good
congressman is putting his name on.

133
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:46,669
Constitution was built
on checks and balances.

134
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:47,962
And the people's will.

135
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:50,548
It's not about who the president is.

136
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:52,550
It's about what the office has become.

137
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:57,388
Gentlemen, if you'll
excuse me for a minute,

138
00:09:57,472 --> 00:10:00,391
I promised Brett here I'd introduce
him to a blue dog Democrat,

139
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,185
assuming I can find one.

140
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:05,825
I never thought I'd see him again.

141
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:06,898
He was in rehab.

142
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:09,317
And is back in the program.

143
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,702
Those charges were dropped,

144
00:10:10,703 --> 00:10:12,987
but he's still got a case chasing him.

145
00:10:13,071 --> 00:10:16,741
If anything, my bet is that
case is chasing the president.

146
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:18,701
Petrov is no longer in the main room.

147
00:10:18,785 --> 00:10:20,995
Secretary Siegerson is
still with Ms. Davis,

148
00:10:21,496 --> 00:10:23,289
while the vice president's exiting.

149
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:27,752
And Homeland Secretary Cafferty was
just whispering with the president.

150
00:10:28,545 --> 00:10:32,549
As for Doug Stamper, he's
with Assistant Director Green.

151
00:10:36,719 --> 00:10:38,471
I want to know who Durant was with,

152
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:41,850
when and where, leading up to the
moment she was pronounced dead.

153
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:44,102
If I start asking around...

154
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:46,688
Questions bring more questions.

155
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:49,440
- Is this an open investigation?
- No.

156
00:10:49,524 --> 00:10:53,027
But for any agent I work
with, I'll be the red flag.

157
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:57,532
Doug, the more I know, the
better it is for both of us.

158
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,243
You trust me?

159
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:05,665
You've always followed through.

160
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:08,126
Then do as I say.

161
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:16,801
But what did you find?

162
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:20,012
Is he talking?

163
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:24,058
All right. Get back to me
when you know anything more.

164
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:25,476
Day or night.

165
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:30,023
Is everything okay?

166
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:32,150
That was about Tom Yates.

167
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:34,444
There's been a recent
charge on his credit card.

168
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:36,487
The Grand Mark in Prague,

169
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:38,531
except it wasn't Tom.

170
00:11:38,615 --> 00:11:41,284
He didn't make the charge.
Or any of the others.

171
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,912
- Somebody stole his...
- His identity.

172
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:48,750
As of now, we have no idea where
the real Tom Yates has been.

173
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:52,545
Well, I hope he's safe.

174
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,339
Wherever he is.

175
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:56,466
Me too.

176
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,020
Oh.

177
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:12,231
Ah.

178
00:12:13,358 --> 00:12:17,028
1945 Mouton-Rothschild.

179
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,280
"V" label.

180
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:26,496
Rothschild commissioned it to
celebrate the Allied victory

181
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,498
in the Great Patriotic War.

182
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,792
You mean World War II.

183
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:35,421
Hmm. I wonder what she
was saving this for.

184
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,468
Should we?

185
00:12:43,513 --> 00:12:47,350
Ah, come on. There must be
some mischief in you somewhere.

186
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:49,894
Do you object?

187
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:52,772
Not my place.

188
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:55,650
And where exactly is your place?

189
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:59,737
I specifically asked to
meet with the president.

190
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:08,788
Hmm. There must be a
corkscrew somewhere, hmm?

191
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:11,749
She wouldn't keep these
bottles in here without one.

192
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:15,003
- When it comes to Syria, Mr. President...
- A moment, please.

193
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:18,171
Sir...

194
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:21,426
our only goal is stability,

195
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:24,012
peace, prosperity for the Syrian people.

196
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:27,557
We need to re-engage. We
need to re-start talks...

197
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,640
Talks?

198
00:13:28,891 --> 00:13:30,268
Talk, talk, talk.

199
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:33,021
While you're busy making
side deals with Nexis

200
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:35,315
and the rest of your Republican friends.

201
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:36,399
The Shepherds.

202
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:39,777
That is who you really
work for, isn't it?

203
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,947
We can freeze assets,

204
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:46,367
put sanctions back into place.

205
00:13:50,705 --> 00:13:52,373
Must be about...

206
00:13:53,041 --> 00:13:55,793
7:30 at night in Damascus.

207
00:13:57,045 --> 00:13:58,463
If we do nothing,

208
00:13:59,005 --> 00:14:02,216
by dawn, skirmishes between
our troops and yours will begin.

209
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:05,928
And once Russian soldiers
start killing American soldiers,

210
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:09,015
the chaos will continue.

211
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:11,683
Or...

212
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:15,063
we can pull out a map of Syria,

213
00:14:15,813 --> 00:14:17,857
right here, right now.

214
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:22,320
And you and I, like
the imperialists we are,

215
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:24,822
can decide who gets what.

216
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,243
Shall we?

217
00:14:30,912 --> 00:14:32,497
I'll speak to the president.

218
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,711
Whoever decides...

219
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:41,881
is who you should speak to.

220
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:50,348
Aww. What a shame.

221
00:14:56,354 --> 00:14:57,563
What a shame.

222
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,842
I talked to Doug. He asked me,

223
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,195
and at first I thought he
was just covering his tracks,

224
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:30,012
as far as the Secretary's death, but...

225
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:32,014
Now I wonder...

226
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:34,684
the nature of his questions.

227
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:37,270
Ma'am, I've made some calls.

228
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,147
There are some inconsistencies.

229
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:40,982
When she left her house. Where she died.

230
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:43,544
- Wait, what are you telling me?
- I'm not saying it isn't true...

231
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:44,568
Just a second, back up.

232
00:15:44,569 --> 00:15:46,446
It's just hard to be
certain is all I'm saying.

233
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:53,786
- I'd like you to go find him.
- I can't talk to him again.

234
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:58,666
My fear is he'll become suspicious.

235
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:01,544
He knows me as someone
who does what he's told.

236
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:04,130
I don't understand, If
it's not him, then...

237
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:06,966
how did she die, for God's sake?

238
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:09,385
Ma'am...

239
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:11,596
I don't know.

240
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:25,776
Mr. Shepherd would like to
be kept informed in real time.

241
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:27,111
It's under control.

242
00:16:27,195 --> 00:16:29,447
Then it shouldn't be a
problem to keep us included.

243
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:32,450
Do you understand how long
I've known the Shepherds?

244
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:35,828
Whatever you discussed with
Petrov needs to be run by him.

245
00:16:35,912 --> 00:16:38,080
Let me enlighten you about
something, Mr. Grayson.

246
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:39,986
I do not need you to convey a message e

247
00:16:39,987 --> 00:16:41,417
between me and Bill Shepherd, okay?

248
00:16:41,501 --> 00:16:44,212
Well, that's preferable,
as long as, and forgive me,

249
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:47,715
you make no decisions when it
comes to Syria without his say-so.

250
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:50,259
- Don't get over your skis, sir.
- We're done here.

251
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:52,803
- I don't think...
- The vice president says we are done.

252
00:16:58,184 --> 00:16:59,435
Doug Stamper.

253
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,982
Linda. How are you?

254
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,194
- You weren't at the funeral.
- I arrived late.

255
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:11,113
Out of politics, I understand?

256
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:13,574
President Walker made
sure I had a soft landing.

257
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:15,993
I'm at a university in Colorado,

258
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:19,497
where the water is fresh
and the air is clean.

259
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:22,333
- Hmm. Sounds dangerous.
- It is.

260
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:24,126
To think that clearly.

261
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:25,920
How are you?

262
00:17:27,088 --> 00:17:28,339
What have you read?

263
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:29,674
About you?

264
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:31,551
Most of it.

265
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,928
The last three months of it.

266
00:17:35,012 --> 00:17:37,265
About your supposed confession.

267
00:17:38,391 --> 00:17:41,143
What more could I possibly add
that you haven't already read?

268
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:44,480
There's what you read,
and there's the truth.

269
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:47,066
I'm not ashamed.

270
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:50,987
The time away led me to
finally realize who I am.

271
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:56,158
Does the congressman know about you?

272
00:17:56,701 --> 00:17:57,701
I mean...

273
00:17:58,119 --> 00:17:59,119
know.

274
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:02,790
With my help he's gonna be the
next speaker of the House...

275
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:05,293
I went to law school
with the US Attorney.

276
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:07,420
She's tired of waiting.

277
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:11,841
She's issuing a subpoena with
your name on it sometime tomorrow.

278
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,760
Tell her what you know.

279
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:18,097
You have a chance to
survive all this, Doug.

280
00:18:23,144 --> 00:18:24,687
Tartus, yes?

281
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:27,732
But the rest of the coast...

282
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:31,611
can we afford to let it go?

283
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:34,780
Goodbye.

284
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:36,271
It could work.

285
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:39,785
Petrov has plans to
expand the Naval base

286
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,245
to the port of Tartus.

287
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:43,623
The only reason he's
propping up the regime

288
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:45,082
is because they control the coast.

289
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:46,709
He needs the ports.

290
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:50,338
Force him to fight for those and
he'll leave the rest of Syria alone.

291
00:18:52,882 --> 00:18:53,882
Mark...

292
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:57,053
the moment is here.

293
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,304
He's here.

294
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:02,035
- It can't wait.
- I still don't understand how agreements

295
00:19:02,036 --> 00:19:03,434
which haven't even been finalized yet...

296
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:05,811
- Doesn't matter. He got wind of it.
- From who?

297
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:08,773
The point is, is he is a greedy...

298
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:12,068
- Motherfucker, yes.
- And greedy motherfuckers always find out.

299
00:19:13,444 --> 00:19:14,862
He's relentless.

300
00:19:17,031 --> 00:19:19,700
I spent two years in
the Kurdish northwest,

301
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:22,161
outfitted rebels in the southeast.

302
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:26,165
I know every angle
Petrov will keep in play.

303
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:30,586
He has a sixth sense when
it comes to hesitation.

304
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,966
If you need me to be in there...

305
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:38,135
You just can't do it, can you?

306
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:40,720
What?

307
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,430
Nothing.

308
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:45,768
- Mark...
- You just can't step back and trust.

309
00:19:46,477 --> 00:19:47,770
I trust you, Mark.

310
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:52,108
But if the backseat president is
gonna take the wheel, you gotta drive.

311
00:19:55,236 --> 00:19:58,072
There's a reason you and I
are alone in the world, Jane.

312
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:03,828
Yes, of course.

313
00:20:06,414 --> 00:20:08,833
- How long?
- A lifetime.

314
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,920
You moved out west, right?
More time with your son.

315
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:14,505
As much as he'll give me.

316
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:17,174
- And is he still enjoying Stan...
- Claire.

317
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,427
Madam President,

318
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:21,887
we don't need to exchange pleasantries.

319
00:20:23,848 --> 00:20:27,435
These days I tend to think a
lot about what might have been.

320
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:30,271
I'd like to apologize.

321
00:20:31,439 --> 00:20:33,524
- For what?
- My one regret.

322
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,944
I should've been there in Gaffney.

323
00:20:37,862 --> 00:20:38,946
Honestly,

324
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,698
it's been haunting me.

325
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,908
There was something he needed to know.

326
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:45,286
It was a mistake.

327
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:49,832
Overlooking Francis
for secretary of state.

328
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:51,751
- Linda, it's water under the bridge.
- No.

329
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:53,794
No.

330
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:56,005
If we hadn't,

331
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:57,631
I don't know.

332
00:20:57,923 --> 00:21:00,134
Maybe everything would
have been different.

333
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:02,970
For who?

334
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:04,388
This country.

335
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:08,601
Obviously, there's no way
for me to tell him that now.

336
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,145
The least I can do is tell you.

337
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:13,439
There is no need for that.

338
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:16,317
How do you expect to separate
yourself from his crimes?

339
00:21:17,318 --> 00:21:21,197
As corrupt as these politics
we put up with have become...

340
00:21:21,739 --> 00:21:25,284
how can the people
against you not use it?

341
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:30,122
You thought you got
away with it all, Claire.

342
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:32,416
But that remains to be seen.

343
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,423
Everything happens exactly as it should.

344
00:21:42,218 --> 00:21:43,218
Nice seeing you.

345
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,567
What are you up to?

346
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:03,405
I'm thinking about mortality.

347
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:06,534
I think a lot of us
are doing that today.

348
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,577
We're about to have a meeting.

349
00:22:08,661 --> 00:22:11,038
I can't be a part of it.
Viktor knows me all too well.

350
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:12,498
I'm on board.

351
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:16,502
Claire, I see you. I told
Mark not to worry about it.

352
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:18,396
But I have an inkling
that's not necessarily...

353
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:20,548
Spare me your inkling, Jane.

354
00:22:22,675 --> 00:22:24,718
This deal is for your own good.

355
00:22:24,802 --> 00:22:26,470
It's about the whole region.

356
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:28,889
Our presence. Our authority.

357
00:22:30,224 --> 00:22:32,852
Mark and Marcy can do the heavy lifting.

358
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:38,190
Help me prevent a war
from happening today.

359
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:42,736
Any more instability and everybody
loses. Help me avert that.

360
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:47,283
I promise you...

361
00:22:48,242 --> 00:22:51,871
I will chip away at Bill
and Annette Shepherd.

362
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:56,375
Because the only way
to truly take them down

363
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:59,753
is one piece at a time.

364
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:07,344
What do you think
really happened to Cathy?

365
00:23:14,852 --> 00:23:16,020
Okay.

366
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:19,481
I guess you got lucky then.

367
00:23:22,151 --> 00:23:23,736
No one is that lucky.

368
00:23:28,032 --> 00:23:30,743
The president is willing to
leave the coast uncontested.

369
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:33,078
- Tartus...
- That port is already ours.

370
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:34,413
And will remain so.

371
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:37,333
We'll keep our forces away
from the entire Western coast.

372
00:23:37,416 --> 00:23:39,710
This will give you unfettered
access to the Mediterranean.

373
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:42,379
- No.
- Sir, the Sixth Fleet is en route.

374
00:23:42,463 --> 00:23:44,006
- No.
- If you want a naval standoff...

375
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:46,300
No! Let's not pretend.

376
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:49,428
What's really at stake here is your
country lining its pockets and...

377
00:23:51,931 --> 00:23:53,182
Madam President,

378
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,808
Mr. President,

379
00:23:55,142 --> 00:23:57,686
- the vice president asked me to join.
- Mr. Grayson...

380
00:23:57,770 --> 00:23:58,938
On behalf of a company

381
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:01,061
- with subsidiaries in the Middle East.
- Excuse me.

382
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:03,359
We want to ensure that
we're part of the solution.

383
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:06,612
This will signal to the
world that Russia is back.

384
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,381
- Russia's back?
- Mr. Vice President,

385
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:11,367
there are terms being negotiated
here that need to be discussed...

386
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:12,534
Christ!

387
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:17,081
If Secretary Durant were here,
we'd be long past this posturing

388
00:24:17,164 --> 00:24:19,833
- and dealing with the real question.
- Yes, peace in the region.

389
00:24:19,917 --> 00:24:21,794
Peace? Really?

390
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:24,713
You want to use peace to decide

391
00:24:24,797 --> 00:24:28,467
who will rebuild this pizdets?

392
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:30,427
I don't understand what that means,

393
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:33,806
- Mr. President.
- That means clusterfuck.

394
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,350
Sir, stability in the
region helps all of us.

395
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:39,061
You want to give me the
West and take the East?

396
00:24:40,104 --> 00:24:41,647
That's a first.

397
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,399
So, here's what I want.

398
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:45,734
The ports, yes, of course.

399
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:47,828
But I also want Russian exclusivity

400
00:24:47,829 --> 00:24:50,323
on all offshore oil and gas exploration.

401
00:24:50,406 --> 00:24:52,908
- I think we need to wait.
- Shut up.

402
00:24:53,534 --> 00:24:55,334
We can't be in a position
where we can get in,

403
00:24:55,369 --> 00:24:56,769
and we can't get our resources out.

404
00:24:56,829 --> 00:24:59,039
If history has taught
us anything, it's that

405
00:24:59,123 --> 00:25:01,291
the Americans always
find a way to leave,

406
00:25:01,375 --> 00:25:03,127
no matter what it costs them.

407
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:04,836
So...

408
00:25:05,963 --> 00:25:08,632
thoughts, Madam President?

409
00:25:12,136 --> 00:25:13,470
Anything?

410
00:25:19,143 --> 00:25:21,270
I concur with the vice president.

411
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,024
Hmm.

412
00:25:28,152 --> 00:25:30,070
I believe we have much to consider.

413
00:25:41,915 --> 00:25:44,626
Playing incompetent is so exhausting.

414
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:48,880
Hey.

415
00:25:48,881 --> 00:25:50,323
Here's a copy of the president's remarks

416
00:25:50,324 --> 00:25:52,110
for the secretary's
memorial this evening.

417
00:25:52,134 --> 00:25:53,635
I already have a copy.

418
00:25:53,719 --> 00:25:55,888
It includes the changes
she made in the car.

419
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:57,765
Right. Thank you.

420
00:26:00,768 --> 00:26:04,313
Hey. Is it true Tom Yates is missing?

421
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:06,023
I believe so.

422
00:26:06,356 --> 00:26:10,527
Oh. Is it true he had an affair
with somebody in the White House?

423
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:12,446
Was it you?

424
00:26:12,738 --> 00:26:14,281
Excuse me.

425
00:26:17,451 --> 00:26:18,660
I'll look through this.

426
00:26:32,341 --> 00:26:33,341
Thank you.

427
00:26:37,221 --> 00:26:39,640
- I don't like liars.
- Me neither.

428
00:26:40,057 --> 00:26:41,284
Why would you let me believe...

429
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:44,436
It seemed like you wanted me to
be the one responsible for Cathy.

430
00:26:44,937 --> 00:26:47,022
That it might be useful to you somehow.

431
00:26:50,234 --> 00:26:53,654
Every time I plan to
quit, something happens.

432
00:26:56,198 --> 00:26:58,909
Francis would certainly
be disappointed in me.

433
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:04,081
Terrible habit.

434
00:27:05,916 --> 00:27:07,876
Helped me though when I quit drinking.

435
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:12,965
Don't say anything to
the US attorney, Doug.

436
00:27:13,048 --> 00:27:14,842
She's working with the Shepherds.

437
00:27:16,218 --> 00:27:19,972
I pardon you tonight, and anything
else she has will be my problem.

438
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:23,892
I'll always be a problem for you.

439
00:27:23,976 --> 00:27:25,811
What do you want from me, Doug?

440
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,397
You're the one with
all the leverage here.

441
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:32,526
Congressman Cole. I'll
put him on my ticket 2020.

442
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:35,362
Mark won't survive, I'm sure of it.

443
00:27:35,696 --> 00:27:38,073
2024, Brett Cole will be the president.

444
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:40,200
And you will be back in the White House.

445
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:44,663
We can make him president,

446
00:27:45,914 --> 00:27:47,708
just like we did with Francis.

447
00:27:49,418 --> 00:27:51,044
Cole will mean a split ticket.

448
00:27:51,837 --> 00:27:54,756
And that might be the very
best thing for this country.

449
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:00,137
Pardon Francis as well.

450
00:28:03,557 --> 00:28:05,559
If I do that, I could get impeached.

451
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:06,642
No.

452
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:10,856
You're a survivor.
You've proven that much.

453
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:13,692
Pardon him as well.

454
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:18,030
Bill's gonna hate anything

455
00:28:18,113 --> 00:28:20,073
even approaching a
partnership with the Kremlin.

456
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:21,867
It's his sister who holds a grudge.

457
00:28:21,950 --> 00:28:23,619
But still, you have no choice.

458
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:28,207
I mean, in my experience, once
the chaos tips into forever,

459
00:28:28,290 --> 00:28:29,291
you've got nothing.

460
00:28:29,374 --> 00:28:31,293
And we're very close to forever.

461
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:37,216
And she said nothing.

462
00:28:39,676 --> 00:28:41,720
It really bothers you, doesn't it?

463
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:43,555
When you can't figure a person out.

464
00:28:44,181 --> 00:28:47,267
- Especially when you're attracted.
- Oh, my God, what are you...

465
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:52,105
I am not involved with Claire Underwood.

466
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,900
I'm talking about Annette.

467
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:58,737
I'm not involved with
anyone at the moment.

468
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:01,573
Every time I see the both of you
together, it brings back memories.

469
00:29:03,784 --> 00:29:06,161
Never thought you'd step
out from behind the scenes.

470
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:08,914
Well, wherever I can do
the most good, Congressman.

471
00:29:08,997 --> 00:29:11,375
He hasn't changed. Not at all.

472
00:29:11,458 --> 00:29:12,918
Blessing and a curse.

473
00:29:14,294 --> 00:29:16,421
I haven't forgotten
everything you did for me.

474
00:29:17,339 --> 00:29:19,841
Oh, you made it to the
House with or without me.

475
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:21,468
You showed me the way.

476
00:29:23,595 --> 00:29:24,638
Well...

477
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,890
I've been meaning to say hello,

478
00:29:27,516 --> 00:29:30,102
ever since you left the party
and went to the other side.

479
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:33,313
Jane.

480
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:42,155
Haven't spoken to him in over a decade.

481
00:29:42,239 --> 00:29:43,365
He knows.

482
00:29:43,448 --> 00:29:45,075
He knows I was involved.

483
00:29:46,076 --> 00:29:47,536
Well, weren't you?

484
00:29:49,329 --> 00:29:50,414
Weren't we?

485
00:29:53,583 --> 00:29:55,711
When's the last time
you were in my house?

486
00:29:58,088 --> 00:29:59,088
Don't.

487
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,635
Mark, I'm not going back there.

488
00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:09,057
No, no, Tom Yates was sleeping
with the new press secretary

489
00:30:09,141 --> 00:30:10,475
in the White House.

490
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,358
He traded the East for the West.

491
00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:22,654
Yes, all offshore oil
and gas exploration, sir.

492
00:30:25,032 --> 00:30:26,592
They're saying we'll still have access,

493
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:28,803
but all shipping through the
Mediterranean will be affected.

494
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:31,621
And there's no denying we'll
be somewhat at their mercy.

495
00:30:34,916 --> 00:30:37,252
Because there wasn't
time to consult you.

496
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:42,071
Petrov upped the ante

497
00:30:42,072 --> 00:30:45,135
and it looks like the vice
president is going to cave.

498
00:30:47,512 --> 00:30:49,973
It's not a complicated
question, Miss Stewart.

499
00:30:50,432 --> 00:30:51,933
Were you sleeping with him?

500
00:30:54,728 --> 00:30:58,357
Do I need to say this administration
has taken a huge chance on you?

501
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:00,817
- Were you sleeping...
- It is none of your business.

502
00:31:00,901 --> 00:31:01,901
Well...

503
00:31:02,361 --> 00:31:04,529
that answers that, then.

504
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:08,950
This is exactly the kind of
thing the White House needs...

505
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:12,537
to avoid.

506
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:19,002
And Tom Yates is missing.

507
00:31:20,337 --> 00:31:22,798
Which only makes the whole
story more problematic.

508
00:31:22,881 --> 00:31:24,761
I have no idea where any
of this is coming from.

509
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:27,928
Well, I suggest you find a more
convincing way of denying it.

510
00:31:28,845 --> 00:31:32,557
Because your inability to
lie is a liability, right?

511
00:31:36,770 --> 00:31:39,147
Now, where is our president?

512
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:45,237
Why didn't you tell them I invited you?

513
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:48,115
You didn't rat me out.

514
00:31:48,198 --> 00:31:50,826
You sound like a
gangster, Madam President.

515
00:31:53,036 --> 00:31:54,454
Curiosity, I suppose.

516
00:31:54,538 --> 00:31:56,790
I wanted to watch you

517
00:31:57,833 --> 00:31:58,875
and hear them.

518
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:03,171
Your vice president is
serving too many masters.

519
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:08,009
Strange, hmm?

520
00:32:09,719 --> 00:32:12,764
Cathy passing away
so soon after Francis.

521
00:32:13,181 --> 00:32:15,183
Death usually comes in threes.

522
00:32:16,685 --> 00:32:19,271
Except when it comes in fours or fives.

523
00:32:20,564 --> 00:32:23,233
Are you free now, Madam President?

524
00:32:25,444 --> 00:32:26,486
Not quite.

525
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:30,740
Were you happy with what they proposed?

526
00:32:31,074 --> 00:32:32,742
Mostly, I'm just curious.`

527
00:32:33,034 --> 00:32:34,870
Hmm. About what?

528
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:38,039
What you're about to offer.
That is why you invited me.

529
00:32:38,540 --> 00:32:40,584
- And that is why I said yes.
- Hmm.

530
00:32:41,501 --> 00:32:43,086
Well, Nexis Securities

531
00:32:43,837 --> 00:32:48,008
or any other contractor
connected to Shepherd Unlimited

532
00:32:48,925 --> 00:32:52,262
will never be allowed in
Syria while I'm president.

533
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,681
That's a strong declaration.

534
00:32:55,557 --> 00:32:58,226
Bids will be contingent on my approval.

535
00:32:59,019 --> 00:33:01,229
You can have the oil and gas, the ports.

536
00:33:01,313 --> 00:33:05,192
And 20% of profits from the
resources passing through.

537
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:07,819
That's...

538
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:10,655
That's quite a taste.

539
00:33:13,617 --> 00:33:15,202
Maybe you are a gangster.

540
00:33:16,912 --> 00:33:18,538
And how will you...

541
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,957
defend your position?

542
00:33:22,876 --> 00:33:23,876
Peace.

543
00:33:26,171 --> 00:33:28,173
Isn't that what our two countries

544
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:30,505
have used to justify what
we've done in the region

545
00:33:30,506 --> 00:33:31,384
for over a hundred years?

546
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:33,345
Peace is overrated, Claire.

547
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:35,430
So are my vice president's promises.

548
00:33:35,514 --> 00:33:37,849
And yet, yours seem too generous.

549
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:47,234
Your husband would have lost himself
in the brightness of this day,

550
00:33:47,317 --> 00:33:49,653
blinded by how he needed to be seen.

551
00:33:50,946 --> 00:33:52,489
That always cost him.

552
00:33:53,657 --> 00:33:54,824
Can I ask?

553
00:33:56,618 --> 00:33:58,286
If you knew this...

554
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:02,082
why did you marry him?

555
00:34:04,417 --> 00:34:05,710
Do you even know?

556
00:34:09,339 --> 00:34:10,715
As it turns out...

557
00:34:11,424 --> 00:34:13,760
my husband was a means to an end.

558
00:34:16,721 --> 00:34:17,721
Hmm.

559
00:34:30,944 --> 00:34:33,321
Tell the people you work for
that I'm not going to testify.

560
00:34:33,405 --> 00:34:35,448
A second.

561
00:34:35,532 --> 00:34:36,532
Seth.

562
00:34:37,993 --> 00:34:39,828
Seth, do you hear me?

563
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:41,580
Back off, Doug.

564
00:34:42,664 --> 00:34:44,708
Whatever you told them,
I'll have no part of it.

565
00:34:45,125 --> 00:34:47,669
The U.S. Attorney can
subpoena me. She can try to...

566
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:52,632
I'm done.

567
00:34:54,551 --> 00:34:57,554
You wouldn't know a good thing
if it smacked you in the face.

568
00:34:59,723 --> 00:35:01,641
I don't know why I'm trying to help you.

569
00:35:04,311 --> 00:35:06,688
You're not in the White
House anymore, Doug.

570
00:35:12,569 --> 00:35:14,362
Oh. Where were you?

571
00:35:14,738 --> 00:35:16,740
Even presidents need to pee, Mark.

572
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,825
Look, there's a rumor flying around.

573
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:21,494
- Was it good?
- It's easily dismissible.

574
00:35:21,578 --> 00:35:23,830
Then I talked to NSA. It's
not gonna work, Claire.

575
00:35:23,913 --> 00:35:27,125
Some White House affair is
not gonna make it go away.

576
00:35:28,418 --> 00:35:30,837
The dead never really stay dead, Mark.

577
00:35:31,713 --> 00:35:33,590
Not for the people who loved them.

578
00:35:46,645 --> 00:35:48,438
- Ah. Excuse me.
- Excuse me.

579
00:35:52,442 --> 00:35:53,985
Did you get taller?

580
00:35:54,611 --> 00:35:55,654
Yes.

581
00:35:56,696 --> 00:35:57,989
So strange

582
00:35:58,073 --> 00:36:01,117
for someone trapped
in a Napoleon complex.

583
00:36:01,201 --> 00:36:05,538
If only your personality
matched your looks, Jane Davis.

584
00:36:08,333 --> 00:36:10,752
I was surprised you left negotiations

585
00:36:10,835 --> 00:36:14,130
to your surrogate Ms. Siegerson.

586
00:36:14,631 --> 00:36:16,633
Always best to speak for oneself.

587
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:18,802
Hmm. That's rich, coming from you.

588
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:21,262
Doublespeak is your mother tongue.

589
00:36:21,346 --> 00:36:23,181
And subterfuge is yours.

590
00:36:23,640 --> 00:36:26,726
You and your agencies, hmm?

591
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:32,065
The CIA is nothing short
of a cultural terrorist.

592
00:36:32,148 --> 00:36:33,148
It's men like you...

593
00:36:33,149 --> 00:36:35,443
Barging into countries
you know nothing about.

594
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:38,571
- You get under my skin.
- Profiting from destabilization.

595
00:36:38,655 --> 00:36:40,907
Leaving nothing but ruin in your wake.

596
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:43,410
- It's chemical, it's...
- And then you're offended...

597
00:36:43,493 --> 00:36:46,371
You're offended when it's
my men, my air strikes,

598
00:36:46,454 --> 00:36:48,099
- that bring some kind of order.
- Chemical!

599
00:36:48,123 --> 00:36:52,252
You are nothing but a
communist in a handmade suit.

600
00:36:52,335 --> 00:36:53,586
A pig!

601
00:36:58,133 --> 00:36:59,759
So emotional.

602
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:03,513
Emotions make deals come apart, Jane.

603
00:37:04,347 --> 00:37:05,390
Tell me,

604
00:37:05,473 --> 00:37:09,310
why should I trust any
deal that involves you?

605
00:37:18,486 --> 00:37:21,197
I will not rest

606
00:37:21,823 --> 00:37:23,908
until you're done, Viktor.

607
00:37:25,952 --> 00:37:27,954
Dead and buried.

608
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:32,083
Bastard!

609
00:37:33,334 --> 00:37:34,461
Then I guess...

610
00:37:37,213 --> 00:37:38,673
you'll never rest.

611
00:37:51,478 --> 00:37:54,647
Okay. My directions were clear.

612
00:37:54,856 --> 00:37:56,775
- No doubt.
- So where's the confusion?

613
00:37:57,150 --> 00:37:59,611
Well, I'm guessing somewhere
between what you wanted to happen

614
00:37:59,694 --> 00:38:01,196
and what had to happen.

615
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,552
If you didn't want me to call Bill, e

616
00:38:02,553 --> 00:38:04,050
you shouldn't have given me a reason to.

617
00:38:04,073 --> 00:38:05,825
There was no place for you in that room.

618
00:38:05,909 --> 00:38:07,509
And unless you show some proper respect,

619
00:38:07,535 --> 00:38:09,370
no place for you in
this whole fucking town.

620
00:38:09,454 --> 00:38:10,663
I'll see to that personally.

621
00:38:10,747 --> 00:38:12,123
I'll keep that in mind.

622
00:38:12,207 --> 00:38:14,959
From now on, stay in your
lane, keep your mouth shut,

623
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:16,753
unless I say otherwise. You got it?

624
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:19,589
Again, coming in clear,

625
00:38:20,507 --> 00:38:21,633
but not a dent.

626
00:38:22,759 --> 00:38:24,594
It's okay, we'll get there.

627
00:38:25,386 --> 00:38:28,181
Even if we don't, fuck do I care?

628
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:30,558
I don't work for you.

629
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:33,478
We both work for him.

630
00:38:39,526 --> 00:38:40,902
Mr. Stamper.

631
00:38:44,113 --> 00:38:48,451
We usually meet under more
orchestrated circumstances.

632
00:38:48,535 --> 00:38:50,745
Not that this isn't
one of those, as well.

633
00:38:52,121 --> 00:38:54,082
Where do you find yourself these days?

634
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:56,709
Consulting for an ambitious Congressman.

635
00:38:56,793 --> 00:38:58,044
Midterms are coming.

636
00:38:58,545 --> 00:38:59,545
I bet...

637
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:03,675
he has no idea how well
you see in the dark.

638
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:07,887
Who do you fear most?

639
00:39:09,222 --> 00:39:10,598
Out of all of them.

640
00:39:14,519 --> 00:39:15,519
Her.

641
00:39:27,073 --> 00:39:29,450
I can't eat at these things, either.

642
00:39:36,499 --> 00:39:38,626
The spread looks lovely. Everything.

643
00:39:39,127 --> 00:39:40,837
You all did right by her.

644
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,422
Well, I didn't do a thing.

645
00:39:43,423 --> 00:39:45,550
Stan took care of all of it.

646
00:39:49,929 --> 00:39:51,306
How you holding up?

647
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:55,768
I can't make sense of it.

648
00:39:57,729 --> 00:39:59,522
My dad went the same way, you know?

649
00:40:01,649 --> 00:40:03,693
Never sick a day in
his life. And then...

650
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:07,822
Right when he was driving,

651
00:40:08,364 --> 00:40:10,408
just drifted onto oncoming traffic.

652
00:40:10,491 --> 00:40:12,535
- Jesus.
- Oh, my goodness.

653
00:40:12,911 --> 00:40:14,454
I had to quickly grab the wheel

654
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:16,289
and swerved us over to the shoulder.

655
00:40:17,332 --> 00:40:18,791
How old were you?

656
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:20,126
Twelve.

657
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,505
Twelve. That's rough.

658
00:40:25,423 --> 00:40:26,633
It's all rough.

659
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:28,718
Twelve. Twenty-one.

660
00:40:29,135 --> 00:40:30,136
Fifty-one.

661
00:40:31,846 --> 00:40:32,972
You're never ready.

662
00:40:40,939 --> 00:40:43,399
Wednesday afternoon she
calls me, as she does.

663
00:40:43,816 --> 00:40:45,109
Said her head hurt.

664
00:40:45,193 --> 00:40:47,487
Like migraine bad, so she...

665
00:40:48,321 --> 00:40:50,782
was headed to her personal doctor.

666
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:55,161
I call back to see how she was doing.

667
00:40:55,244 --> 00:40:56,955
Stan hits me with it.

668
00:40:58,539 --> 00:41:01,292
She didn't even make it to the
office. It happened in the car.

669
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:04,379
So, I got on the first flight out.

670
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:06,798
Hey, it's okay.

671
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:08,299
Doug's right.

672
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:11,135
It's fine, let it out.

673
00:41:16,516 --> 00:41:18,893
By the time I landed, it was all done.

674
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:21,938
Body was...

675
00:41:23,022 --> 00:41:25,358
whatever, at the place...

676
00:41:26,651 --> 00:41:27,735
to get cremated.

677
00:41:28,945 --> 00:41:30,738
No autopsy, nothing.

678
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:32,991
Stan made it happen so fast.

679
00:41:38,788 --> 00:41:42,291
And I'm the only one who can't keep
his shit together. But it's just...

680
00:41:43,334 --> 00:41:47,630
I never got the chance to see her.

681
00:41:50,049 --> 00:41:52,635
To say goodbye.

682
00:41:52,719 --> 00:41:54,519
I'm sorry. You all didn't
ask for any of this.

683
00:41:54,887 --> 00:41:57,015
- No. Please.
- We get it.

684
00:41:58,182 --> 00:42:02,145
Yes, Doug Stamper and the
president seem very much in sync.

685
00:42:03,938 --> 00:42:06,556
- Mm-hmm.
- I was hoping to attend

686
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:08,568
the secretary's memorial as well,

687
00:42:08,651 --> 00:42:10,486
but my time is limited.

688
00:42:10,570 --> 00:42:13,031
It was meaningful that
you traveled all this way.

689
00:42:13,114 --> 00:42:15,116
I've been thinking about
what you said to me.

690
00:42:17,994 --> 00:42:19,162
I accept.

691
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:22,749
I'm so happy to hear that.

692
00:42:24,417 --> 00:42:26,502
One other thing. Tom Yates.

693
00:42:27,920 --> 00:42:30,506
Your government was behind
whatever happened to him.

694
00:42:44,687 --> 00:42:47,148
Presidents aren't allowed to be human.

695
00:42:47,231 --> 00:42:49,942
You have to choose. Power or love.

696
00:42:50,610 --> 00:42:52,820
That was very clear from the beginning.

697
00:42:54,072 --> 00:42:55,656
Forgive me, Tom Yates.

698
00:42:56,032 --> 00:43:01,120
I'm about to drag you through
the mud to deny we ever happened.

699
00:43:01,829 --> 00:43:04,624
I'm killing you for the second time.

700
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:07,877
One day, you'll rest in peace.

701
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:09,087
Madam President.

702
00:43:11,130 --> 00:43:13,925
Ma'am, I have to tell you

703
00:43:14,550 --> 00:43:16,844
- there are rumors circulating...
- I know, I know.

704
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:20,807
- If you need me to resign...
- Kelsey, you're not going anywhere.

705
00:43:24,727 --> 00:43:27,127
You can stay at my place
as long as you like.

706
00:43:27,814 --> 00:43:29,190
I appreciate it.

707
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:31,400
Two weeks in Bellport

708
00:43:31,484 --> 00:43:32,610
tapped me out.

709
00:43:33,111 --> 00:43:35,530
Well, your paper will
cover some of that.

710
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:38,157
They don't do expenses, Tom.

711
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:44,080
And my mom didn't have much to leave.

712
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:47,667
I liked the piece.

713
00:43:48,835 --> 00:43:49,835
It was strong.

714
00:43:50,795 --> 00:43:52,421
What's your follow-up?

715
00:43:52,505 --> 00:43:55,550
Well, it's not like anybody
at the EPA can confirm.

716
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:58,511
Well, if the emails exist,
they went to somebody.

717
00:43:58,594 --> 00:44:01,639
Yeah, but my only source
won't return my calls.

718
00:44:02,515 --> 00:44:06,144
He's gotta show up to work every
day. He's afraid. He should be.

719
00:44:10,815 --> 00:44:12,191
Follow up with the app.

720
00:44:13,192 --> 00:44:17,572
Grayson was there, signing up
people who were very scared.

721
00:44:18,239 --> 00:44:19,740
They took advantage of a crisis.

722
00:44:19,824 --> 00:44:22,743
- The Shepherds.
- It's unethical, but it's not illegal.

723
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:26,414
Oh, shit.

724
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:29,250
They shut down Pennsylvania Avenue.

725
00:44:35,339 --> 00:44:37,967
It says to take Massachusetts.

726
00:44:39,010 --> 00:44:40,010
All right.

727
00:44:43,890 --> 00:44:46,058
It's Cathy Durant's memorial today.

728
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:51,230
The bodies are adding up.

729
00:44:56,360 --> 00:45:00,031
Tom, from the very beginning,
we did what we thought was right.

730
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:05,453
At the time, anyway.

731
00:45:05,828 --> 00:45:07,588
Is that how we ended
up in this car together?

732
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:09,373
Look, you cannot blame yourself for...

733
00:45:09,457 --> 00:45:10,875
For not doing enough. Why not?

734
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:12,043
Why shouldn't I?

735
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:13,126
Rachel Posner?

736
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:16,047
Somebody with her name is bouncing
checks in and around New Mexico.

737
00:45:16,130 --> 00:45:18,382
Yeah. And if it leads to nowhere?

738
00:45:23,596 --> 00:45:25,348
Will you ever be able to...

739
00:45:25,848 --> 00:45:26,848
leave it?

740
00:45:27,850 --> 00:45:29,852
If the truth starts to fade away?

741
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:32,605
Truthfully...

742
00:45:36,067 --> 00:45:37,193
I don't know.

743
00:45:44,784 --> 00:45:47,787
I just heard from Bugayev. 20%?

744
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:52,833
I haven't told Mark and the rest
yet. Just know you'll be crucified.

745
00:45:52,917 --> 00:45:55,002
Yes, and how will I feel the difference?

746
00:45:55,836 --> 00:45:57,880
You shouldn't have excluded me.

747
00:46:05,513 --> 00:46:07,556
What's going on with you and Claire?

748
00:46:09,016 --> 00:46:11,978
Look, I can only assume
while you were away

749
00:46:12,061 --> 00:46:14,397
somebody broke down the
definition of insanity.

750
00:46:14,897 --> 00:46:16,607
If not, here's a refresher.

751
00:46:17,066 --> 00:46:21,612
Doing the same shit over and over
and expecting different results.

752
00:46:23,739 --> 00:46:25,616
Yeah, I don't know what she told you

753
00:46:25,700 --> 00:46:27,493
to induce such amnesia,

754
00:46:27,952 --> 00:46:30,329
but if you're seriously
looking down that road again,

755
00:46:30,413 --> 00:46:33,249
there is something that you
should know about Francis' will.

756
00:46:34,041 --> 00:46:35,584
Has she told you what's in it?

757
00:46:36,585 --> 00:46:37,795
Who told you?

758
00:46:38,254 --> 00:46:40,881
If I were you, that's not the
question I'd be asking right now.

759
00:46:41,299 --> 00:46:45,469
I'd be asking, "Why is she
keeping me from the truth?"

760
00:46:47,638 --> 00:46:49,890
He left you more than those cuff links.

761
00:46:52,518 --> 00:46:53,978
You're welcome, Doug.

762
00:47:02,278 --> 00:47:03,654
President Underwood,

763
00:47:03,738 --> 00:47:04,864
Brett Cole.

764
00:47:04,947 --> 00:47:06,532
Yes, I know who you are.

765
00:47:07,033 --> 00:47:08,367
I'll take that as a compliment.

766
00:47:08,868 --> 00:47:11,245
Madam President, you should
make your way to the stage.

767
00:47:11,329 --> 00:47:12,788
Yes, of course. Thank you.

768
00:47:12,872 --> 00:47:13,872
Doug.

769
00:47:15,916 --> 00:47:18,210
- Speak soon?
- Yes, ma'am.

770
00:47:20,338 --> 00:47:21,672
Anything you need to tell me now?

771
00:47:22,048 --> 00:47:23,716
Nope, nothing.

772
00:47:25,634 --> 00:47:27,928
That story about your
father, is that true?

773
00:47:31,849 --> 00:47:32,975
Does it matter?

774
00:47:33,517 --> 00:47:35,686
Well, if it's true, it explains a lot.

775
00:47:36,937 --> 00:47:39,231
If it's not, it explains a lot.

776
00:47:52,328 --> 00:47:53,829
- Thank you for coming.
- Sorry.

777
00:47:53,913 --> 00:47:55,164
I appreciate it.

778
00:47:56,707 --> 00:47:57,707
So sorry.

779
00:48:00,336 --> 00:48:01,462
Good to see you.

780
00:48:27,113 --> 00:48:31,117
To weather the slings and
arrows of 30 years of service

781
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:33,411
and not lose a fraction

782
00:48:33,494 --> 00:48:36,414
of one's signature grit and integrity,

783
00:48:36,831 --> 00:48:38,707
that's not a legacy,

784
00:48:39,417 --> 00:48:40,835
that's a miracle.

785
00:48:41,460 --> 00:48:44,964
But Catherine Durant wasn't
just a Secretary of State.

786
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:47,091
She was a sister.

787
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:50,469
Why isn't someone on
the house right now?

788
00:48:51,345 --> 00:48:53,139
Well, then you heard wrong.

789
00:48:53,222 --> 00:48:55,182
That's right. Day and night.

790
00:48:55,641 --> 00:48:57,370
Yes, every second

791
00:48:57,371 --> 00:49:00,855
until he is on the C-130 to Switzerland.

792
00:49:00,938 --> 00:49:02,940
No, no, no. No ETAs.

793
00:49:03,023 --> 00:49:04,525
Hard dates and times.

794
00:49:05,818 --> 00:49:06,819
Mm-hmm.

795
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:10,781
Mm-hmm. Correct.

796
00:49:11,991 --> 00:49:15,244
No. I'll be the one to
intercept him in Annecy.

797
00:49:15,828 --> 00:49:18,998
Yes, of course. As soon as the money
is wired, you'll be taken care of.

798
